This function is already minimal, so any gain will be small. The rewrite reads the `profile` pointer and `profileIndex` into locals once. It then marks the null/out-of-range path as unlikely, so the common path is a straight load. Behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumSubFields(void) const
{
    const auto* const mesg = profile;
    const FIT_UINT16 idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect((mesg == NULL) || (idx >= mesg->numFields), 0))
        return 0;
    return mesg->fields[idx].numSubFields;
}
```